Package: deferrable-reboot
Version: 25.318.78466~45aac91
Depends: libc, lua, lime-system
Source: /feed/packages/deferrable-reboot
SourceName: deferrable-reboot
Section: utils
SourceDateEpoch: 1763156866
Maintainer: Santiago Piccinini <spiccinini@altermundi.net>
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: 20480
Filename: deferrable-reboot_25.318.78466~45aac91_all.ipk
Size: 2446
SHA256sum: 9d79bc46dd0afc6883c4bd50528cb111b58260f800324fb08cf19449e73ef41b
Description:  This deferrable-reboot provides a deferrable reboot mechanism. The system
 will be rebooted when the uptime of the system reach a specified amount
 of seconds and if /tmp/deferrable-reboot.defer file does not contain a
 number that is greater than the current uptime.
 This way if anyone wants to postpone the reboot, the way is to store the
 next checkpoint in seconds. For example if the system must not reboot from
 now and up to 120 seconds in the future then something like this can be donde
 awk '{print  + 120}' /proc/uptime > /tmp/deferrable-reboot.defer

